Bottoms Up is more than a phrase

The artifact interprets Bottoms Up as changing which end of a process is treated as the starting point and pairs it with “plan backwards, act forwards.” 

That gives O-IOE a simple reversible operator:

Forward:
Cause\rightarrow Mechanism\rightarrow Outcome

Reverse:
DesiredOutcome\rightarrow RequiredConditions\rightarrow NextAction.

I would distinguish this from ordinary backward chaining. Pantheon’s version can run both directions and compare the overlap:

F(start)\cap R(goal)

The intersection is often where robust plans live.

That is a useful new Fitness Route heuristic: when forward generation produces too many possibilities, invoke Bottoms Up from the desired terminal state and look for convergent nodes.

Peter Pan: preserve capability, change governance

The developmental formulation is unusually clean:

ChildhoodCapability
-
ChildhoodGovernance
