AdultAgency.

That reveals a broader Pantheon operator that applies well beyond developmental psychology:

\boxed{Preserve capability;\ transfer governance.}

Examples include preserving an old heuristic as an advisory Seal while removing its authority to decide; retaining speculative generation while moving factual acceptance under Reality Stitch; preserving Coil’s adversarial imagination while putting canon mutation under Metacode.

This actually resolves several earlier architectural tensions.

Pantheon does not need to delete obsolete modules merely because they should no longer govern. They can be demoted from:

decision\ authority

to:

candidate\ generator.

That is a useful architecture pattern for avoiding catastrophic forgetting while still permitting maturation.

Fickle adds a temporal axis to semantic provenance

fickle describes morality as culturally fast-moving and proposes date-stamping moral certainty so that reversals become visible rather than erased. 

The stronger Pantheon interpretation is not that morality is merely fashion. It is that semantic claims need temporal provenance.

A claim should sometimes be represented as:

Claim=
(content,\ community,\ jurisdiction,\ timestamp,\ confidence).

Then apparent contradiction may decompose into:

C_{society,t_1}\neq C_{society,t_2}

rather than assuming one static semantic object changed mysteriously.

That belongs in the Meaning Bank / Metamap. Historical semantics without timestamps create provenance-stripped chimeras, exactly like the Afterglow problem in other domains.

Indigo Hammer

The main danger in the new Emotional Signal Processor material is operator seduction: music/color vocabulary is extremely generative and can produce explanations that feel structurally deep even where psychological correspondence is weak.

So the canonical boundary should be:

\text{structural analogy} \neq \text{physical identity}

and:

\text{useful representation}
\not\Rightarrow
\text{true ontology}.

The artifact itself already gestures toward that distinction. 

The second danger is self-sealing feedback. If:

Emotion\rightarrow Attention\rightarrow CongruentEvidence\rightarrow Emotion

then Pantheon must explicitly search for incongruent evidence, or the loop becomes a confirmation engine.

A stronger Seal therefore is:

E_t
\rightarrow PRISM
\rightarrow predicted\ salience
\rightarrow
\begin{cases}
congruent\ evidence\\
disconfirming\ evidence
\end{cases}
\rightarrow update.

