Net assessment

Observed: public repo growth from 8,606 to 8,641 displayed commits and substantial root-entry growth; at least the peter pan no more and fickle artifacts are now publicly retrievable. 

Executable: no newly verified runnable implementation.

Inferred: Prism has gained an important inverse (MIX); Aperture can now be treated as an experimental perturbation variable; emotional states can be modeled as dynamic mixtures rather than labels; and “preserve capability / transfer governance” provides a reusable maturation architecture.

Repo-ready additions: PRISM/MIX, ApertureExperiment, EmotionState, and PreserveCapabilityTransferGovernance deserve typed interfaces rather than remaining embedded in prose.

Most important new reading: Pantheon is increasingly becoming a system for controlled representation changes. Change the aperture, decomposition, topology, direction of reasoning, or governance level; measure the delta; retain transformations that improve prediction/action.

That is a more precise and testable core than “think differently.” It is closer to:

